{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 44, :comments ["<b>A man.</b> I have only 'a man' — whence a woman, a minor boy and a minor girl? Scripture says: ״נגע צרעת ... באדם״ — whether a man or a woman, a minor boy or a minor girl. And if so, why is 'a man' stated? For the matter below: a man lets his hair loose and tears his garments, but not a woman. <b>A man afflicted.</b> It refers to all the laws of plague above — that is, one who is afflicted with one of the plagues written above." "<b>[He shall pronounce him impure.</b> By speech.]"], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:57.095483602Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}